{
 "format": "estate-crucible-horror/1",
 "id": "H-0094",
 "title": "OUTPUT JCL statements at job and step level, referenced by the OUTPUT parameter of sysout DD statements",
 "category": "jcl",
 "issue": 4891,
 "shapes": [
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDOUT.jcl: job-level //OUT1 OUTPUT DEST=NYC01,CLASS=A and //OUT2 OUTPUT CONTROL=DOUBLE before the first EXEC",
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDOUT.jcl OUT010: step-level //LOCAL OUTPUT COPIES=2 after the EXEC; RPTOUT DD SYSOUT=A,OUTPUT=(*.OUT1,*.OUT2,*.LOCAL)",
  "BDLD jcl/BDLDOUT.jcl OUT020: SYSUT2 DD SYSOUT=A,OUTPUT=*.OUT010.LOCAL (a reference to a step-level OUTPUT statement of an earlier step)"
 ],
 "asserts": "Each OUTPUT JCL statement is one jcl_outputs fact: name, params (the keywords coded), line, and step null for a job-level statement or the step it appears in. An OUTPUT statement is not a step (no jcl_steps fact) and not a DD (no jcl_dds fact). The sysout DDs that name them carry output_refs, the references in the order coded. OUT1, OUT2 and LOCAL are not datasets: no jcl_datasets fact.",
 "citations": [
  {
   "doc": "z/OS MVS JCL Reference (z/OS 2.2.0)",
   "section": "Chapter 12. DD statement > DD: OUTPUT > Purpose",
   "url": "https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SSLTBW_2.2.0/pdf/iea3b611.pdf",
   "quote": "Use the OUTPUT parameter with the SYSOUT parameter to associate a sysout data set explicitly with an OUTPUT JCL statement."
  },
  {
   "doc": "z/OS MVS JCL Reference (z/OS 2.2.0)",
   "section": "Chapter 23. OUTPUT JCL statement > Location in the JCL",
   "url": "https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SSLTBW_2.2.0/pdf/iea3b611.pdf",
   "quote": "Job-level OUTPUT JCL statements: This statement appears after the JOB statement and before the first EXEC statement."
  },
  {
   "doc": "z/OS MVS JCL Reference (z/OS 2.2.0)",
   "section": "Chapter 23. OUTPUT JCL statement > Location in the JCL",
   "url": "https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SSLTBW_2.2.0/pdf/iea3b611.pdf",
   "quote": "Step-level OUTPUT JCL statements: This statement appears in a step, that is, anywhere after the first EXEC statement in a job, except within a concatenated DD statement."
  },
  {
   "doc": "z/OS MVS JCL Reference (z/OS 2.2.0)",
   "section": "Chapter 12. DD statement > DD: OUTPUT > Subparameter definition",
   "url": "https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/SSLTBW_2.2.0/pdf/iea3b611.pdf",
   "quote": "Refers to an earlier OUTPUT JCL statement, name, in this step or an earlier step, stepname, in the same job."
  }
 ],
